@lens(user, developer)
@display("Specs and projects")
specs_and_projects: concept {
  | A spec says what a system does, as seen from outside: its actors, rules, terms, APIs,
  | commands and stories. It never says how the code is built, so it can be read, reviewed
  | and versioned on its own.
  |
  | A project is code with a path, declared with `project` or, for an implementation of a
  | spec, with `implements`. A project's tree holds what's about the code: the components
  | that realize the spec's parts, the tests that prove its rules, what's still planned,
  | and its releases.
  |
  | The two can share a repository or live apart. Apart, the spec is a [sealed package](#language.specifications.implementations.sealed_package) that
  | each implementation imports at a version: [keep a spec apart from its implementation](#learn.howtos.split_spec_and_implementation)
  | shows how.
}
